---
/**
 * About page (/about) — Trevor's bio.
 *
 * Uses BaseLayout for the shared shell; provides only the page content.
 * Copy supplied by Trevor; kept in his own voice.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Trevor Stevens"
  description="About Trevor Stevens (a.k.a. Stanferd) — Air Force reservist, home-lab tinkerer, and self-taught developer learning AI, full-stack, and DevOps."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">About</h1>

  <!--
    prose-style spacing without the Tailwind typography plugin: each paragraph
    gets top margin and relaxed line height for comfortable reading.
  -->
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      Hello, my name is Trevor, but I sometimes go by Stanferd. I grew up in a
      small town in central California. From the start, I had a keen interest in
      computers and electronics.
    </p>
    <p>
      After high school I enlisted in the U.S. Air Force and shipped off to train
      as a flight engineer. After about a year of flight school, I was stationed
      in Tucson, AZ, flying the HH-60 Pavehawk helicopter. Our main mission is
      combat search and rescue, but we also pick up our share of civil rescues
      when we're not deployed. I've completed multiple tours to Iraq,
      Afghanistan, and the Horn of Africa.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've lived in Tucson since 2006 and still work full-time as an Air Force
      reservist.
    </p>
    <p>
      Off alert, and not spending time with family, I tinker with my computers
      and networking equipment. Over the years I've built a solid home lab, which
      I use to host services locally and work toward becoming a network engineer.
      I'm also teaching myself full-stack web development and DevOps. But lately
      my obsession has been agentic AI, LLMs, and &ldquo;vibe coding&rdquo;.
    </p>
    <p>
      I hold a Bachelor of Applied Science in Network Operations from the
      University of Arizona, and an Associate of Applied Science in Systems
      Administration/Networking with a core concentration in cybersecurity.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
